<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mīnōis</span></b> ,
		ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μινωἷς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A female descendant of Minos</i>. So <i>his daughter Ariadne</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8,
				174</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3, 19, 27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grex magis, an regnum Minoida sollicitat?</span>”
				i. e. <i>Pasiphaë, the wife of Minos</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 12, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A name of the Isle of Paros</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				22, § 67</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
